        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tanya Donelly, Trace Cyrus, Mason Musso, Kim Deal, Kristin Hersh, Spencer Steffan\n- Bands: Throwing Muses, The Breeders, Pixies, Metro Station\n- Places: Newport, Rhode Island, New England\n- Roles: singer-songwriters, guitarists, musicians\n\nFacts:\n- Tanya Donelly was born on July 14, 1966, in Newport, Rhode Island.\n- Tanya Donelly is an American Grammy Award-nominated singer-songwriter and guitarist based in New England.\n- Tanya Donelly co-founded Throwing Muses with her stepsister Kristin Hersh.\n- The Breeders are an American alternative rock band formed in 1989 by Kim Deal of the Pixies and Tanya Donelly of Throwing Muses.\n- Trace Cyrus was born Neil Timothy Helson on February 24, 1989.\n- Trace Cyrus is an American musician.\n- Mason Musso was born on March 17, 1989.\n- Mason Musso is an American singer-songwriter and musician.\n- Mason Musso is best known for being part of Metro Station with Trace Cyrus and Spencer Steffan.",
